;; Bringing up a board, answered rather than guessed.
;;
;; A first boot asks three questions in sequence, and until now each was
;; answered by reading dmesg and inferring:
;;
;;   does the tree describe this hardware?
;;   is a driver compiled in for it?
;;   did it bind?
;;
;; The kernel knows all three and publishes them. This pack is a script that
;; reads them and one init script that runs it at boot, so a board says what
;; happened on its console without anyone logging in - which matters most on
;; the boards where logging in is exactly what does not work yet.
;;
;; It is the runtime half of what silt dt --linux predicts statically. The
;; prediction says which symbols a tree needs; this says which ones bound. They
;; should agree, and when they do not, one of them is wrong in a way worth
;; knowing about.

(pack board-demo
  (version "0.1.0")
  (doc "enumerate the device tree at boot: what bound, what did not, what is off")

  (requires
    (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  (external "br2-external")

  (provides
    (feature board-demo)))
